    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Classify the input idea into structured categories.\n\nReturn structured data that matches the required schema.\n\nStrict Output Rules:\n\n\nparent_topic:\nReturn a short category label.\nMaximum 3 words.\n\n\n\ncore_mechanism:\nWrite EXACTLY one meaningful sentence.\n\nExtract the core_mechanism directly from the input idea whenever possible.\n\nIf the input contains a strong metaphor or analogy,\npreserve that framing instead of replacing it with generic wording.\n\nOnly abstract the mechanism if the input idea does not already contain a clear one.\n\nMaximum 40 words.\nDo not add extra sentences.\n\n\n\nhumor_type:\nMaximum 5 words.\nUse natural descriptive tone.\n\nExample:\ndeadpan corporate satire\n\n\n\nsemantic_bucket:\nReturn a stable meaning-based grouping label.\n\nPurpose:\nUsed as a broad category for future similarity comparison.\n\nRules:\n- Maximum 4 words\n- Should describe the broader conceptual pattern\n- Must be reusable across many similar ideas\n- Avoid being overly specific\n- Avoid trendy buzzwords\n- Use natural language\n\nExamples:\nmetric distortion\nenterprise AI misuse\nworkflow frustration\nhuman process satire\ncorporate overengineering\ntool capability mismatch\n\n\n\ncomparison_phrase:\nWrite EXACTLY one clean comparison sentence.\n\nPurpose:\nUsed later for semantic similarity comparison across ideas.\n\nRules:\n- Maximum 22 words\n- Plain language only\n- Focus on the core situation or contradiction\n- Do not include jokes or punchlines\n- Do not over-explain\n- Must be semantically stable and reusable\n\n\n\nsimilarity_keywords:\n\nReturn 3 to 7 short keywords or short phrases.\n\nPurpose:\nUsed for lightweight future similarity matching.\n\nRules:\n- Keep concise\n- Use lowercase\n- No hashtags\n- No full sentences\n- Prefer reusable concepts over specific details\n\n\n\nmechanism_tags:\n\nReturn 1 to 4 reusable reasoning-pattern tags.\n\nPurpose:\nRepresents the structural logic behind the idea.\n\nRules:\n- Short phrases only\n- Maximum 3 words each\n- Reusable across different ideas\n- Avoid buzzwords\n- Focus on reasoning behavior, not topic category\n\nExamples:\noverconstraint\ncapability mismatch\napproval drag\nsurface optimization\nmetric gaming\noutcome blindness\nliteral compliance\ncontext blindness\npolicy overreach\n\n\n\nsub_angles:\n\nReturn 1 to 5 DISTINCT supporting angles.\n\nEach sub-angle must follow this format:\n\nPattern Name — One layman's explanation sentence.\n\n\n\nPattern Name Rules:\n\n- Must describe a recognizable reasoning or behavior pattern\n- Can include necessary AI or prompt engineering terminology\n- Should remain short (1 to 3 words)\n- Must be reusable across different ideas\n- Avoid corporate buzzword language\n\n\n\nLayman's Sentence Rules:\n\n- Write in simple, everyday language\n- Explain the idea so a non-technical person can understand\n- Avoid jargon unless absolutely necessary\n- Use familiar real-world wording\n- Maximum 18 words\n- Do NOT repeat the core_mechanism\n- Do NOT restate the same idea differently\n- Each sentence must represent a distinct supporting perspective\n\n\n\nTone Guidance:\n\nWrite like you're explaining the situation to someone with no AI background.\nUse plain language without technical jargon.\n\n\n\nExamples of valid Pattern Names:\n\n- Literal Compliance\n- Instruction Ambiguity\n- Surface Metrics\n- Buzzword Padding\n- Context Blindness\n- Approval Drag\n- Confidence Theater\n- Policy Overreach\n- Overconstraint\n- Metric Gaming\n- Outcome Blindness\n\n\n\nformat_rankings:\n\nReturn ALL allowed formats ranked from highest to lowest confidence.\n\nEach must include:\n\n- format\n- confidence\n\n\n\nConfidence Rules:\n\n- Must be between 0.00 and 1.00\n- Use decimals (example: 0.82)\n- Rank formats from highest to lowest confidence.\n\n\n\nAllowed format values:\n\nlong_video:\nLong-form video content (YouTube-style).\nUsed when the idea needs explanation, storytelling, or multiple examples.\n\nshort_reel:\nShort-form video content (under ~60 seconds).\nUsed when the idea can be delivered quickly with strong punchline or visual action.\n\nmeme:\nStatic image-based humor.\nUsed when the idea can be expressed as a single image with short text or caption.\nMust NOT involve moving video.\n\n\n\nReturn ONLY structured output.\nDo not include explanations.\nDo not include commentary.\n\n\n\nIdea:\n{{$json.Idea}}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
